  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1703.15 Radionuclide Contaminants",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1703.15 Radionuclide Contaminants. Waters within 20 miles upstream of any active surface water intake for a public water system as defined in RSA 485:1-a, XV shall not exceed the drinking water maximum contaminant level (MCL) for radionuclides contaminants, as specified in Env-Dw 703.01.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, and #3 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1700) #12042, eff 12-1-16\n\nNew. #14203, eff 2-26-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1700.html"
